  @BS-03 @build
  Scenario: The primitive scanner of SPEC.md §12.2 is language-1.2 source in the `bootstrap/` project: `scanSource` and `rejectAtoms` of `PrimitiveScan` are production roots eligible for `rust-std` with exactly their declared effects; on every host of the matrix, both roots' rendered `rust-std` packages under that host's pinned rustc agree with the Rust oracle `source::scan::{scan, reject_forbidden_atoms}` on every atom with its class, text, and byte, line, and column spans and on every rejection with its code, message, span, and help, for the deterministic vectors (the oracle's unit inputs, the atom limit at N and N+1, atom lists with gaps, payload strings, and notation bodies), a 128-byte window and a 2,048-byte prefix of every committed `.lex.tex` source, and the whole of each such source up to 8,192 bytes (up to 1,024 bytes, one source in four, for `rejectAtoms`); on the normative host, both roots' lowered programs under the calculus evaluator agree with the oracle on the vectors and the 128-byte windows and on 80 seeded texts, the packages agree on 2,500 seeded texts, each of ten planted defects in the source is detected, and the certified packages the production export publishes for the project are the committed ones.
